> On the 9other hand, many European
> languages do have a common SOV pattern -- with
> pronoun objects for example.  

But the term SOV (and the five other permutations of S, V, and O) are the 
*basic* order.  The order with pronouns is secondary and does not count toward 
making the language SOV.  French, for instance, is SVO, despite the fact that 
object pronouns usually precede the verb.

